IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-part2-inspection`

-- Tests for sgh-part2-inspection.l4 (ss 8A to 8D). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 8A(1) and (2): the power to require books to be produced`
-- (test alias a8a1 = `s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books`)
-- arguments: the Minister is satisfied there is good reason; the books relate to the affairs of a corporation
#ASSERT `s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason for so doing, the Minister may ... give directions ... to produce such books relating to the affairs of a corporation"
#ASSERT `s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the Minister is not satisfied: a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied and other books: the gate fails first
#ASSERT `s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- satisfied but the books do not relate to the affairs of a corporation: the power is over "such books relating to the affairs of a corporation"
-- (test alias a8a2 = `s 8A(2) the Minister or the authorised person has the like power to require the person to produce the books`)
-- arguments: has power under subsection (1) to require production from a corporation; the person appears to be in possession of the books
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the Minister or the authorised person has the like power to require the person to produce the books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Minister or that authorised person has the like power to require production of those books from any person who appears ... to be in possession of them"
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the Minister or the authorised person has the like power to require the person to produce the books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no power under (1): a failed "where"
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the Minister or the authorised person has the like power to require the person to produce the books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person does not appear to be in possession: the text does not say
-- (test alias a8a3 = `s 8A(2) the production of the books is without prejudice to the lien`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the production of the books is without prejudice to the lien` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "where any such person claims a lien on any books produced by the person, the production is without prejudice to the lien"
#ASSERT `s 8A(2) the production of the books is without prejudice to the lien` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no lien claimed: the text does not say

§ `s 8A(3) to (5)`
-- (test alias a8a31 = `s 8A(3)(a)(i) the power includes making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(a)(i) the power includes making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) if the books are produced -- (i) to make copies of, or take extracts from, them"
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(a)(i) the power includes making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are not produced: the power "includes" and the list is open
-- (test alias a8a32 = `s 8A(3)(a)(ii) the power includes requiring the person to provide an explanation of the books`)
-- arguments: the books are produced; the person is a present or past officer of the corporation or is or was employed by it
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(a)(ii) the power includes requiring the person to provide an explanation of the books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(ii) to require that person who is a present or past officer of, or who is or was at any time employed by the corporation to provide an explanation of any of them"
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(a)(ii) the power includes requiring the person to provide an explanation of the books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person who is neither: the text does not say
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(a)(ii) the power includes requiring the person to provide an explanation of the books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are not produced
-- (test alias a8a33 = `s 8A(3)(b) the power includes requiring the person to state where the books are`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(b) the power includes requiring the person to state where the books are` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) if the books are not produced, to require the person required to produce them to state, to the best of the person's knowledge and belief, where they are"
#ASSERT `s 8A(3)(b) the power includes requiring the person to state where the books are` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are produced: the power "includes" and the list is open
-- (test alias a8a4 = `s 8A(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person who made it`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person who made it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A statement made by a person in compliance with a requirement imposed by this section may be used in evidence against the person"
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person who made it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a statement made otherwise: the subsection does not speak
-- (test alias a8a5 = `s 8A(5) the power to make the requirement extends to the individual`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(5) the power to make the requirement extends to the individual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a body corporate in the course of being wound up (or dissolved) and an individual who is or has been its officer
#ASSERT `s 8A(5) the power to make the requirement extends to the individual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an officer of the body corporate
#ASSERT `s 8A(5) the power to make the requirement extends to the individual` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person is not (or was not) a body corporate

§ `s 8A(6) to (8): the offences, the defence and the penalties`
-- (test alias a8a6 = `s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`)
-- arguments: a requirement was imposed by virtue of section 8A; the requirement was complied with
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "If a requirement ... imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty of an offence"
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- complied with: an element is unmet (split site (i))
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no requirement was imposed: an element is unmet
-- (test alias a8a6p = `s 8A(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 6, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty: no penalty stated
#ASSERT `s 8A(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no requirement imposed: no penalty stated
-- (test alias a8a7 = `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts`)
-- arguments: charged under (6); the requirement was to produce books; proves the books were not in the person's possession or control; proves it was not reasonably practicable to comply
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "it is a defence to prove that they were not in the person's possession or under the person's control"
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement"
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both proved
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither proved: this section gives no defence on these facts (delegated-defences ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not charged under (6): a failed "Where a person is charged"
#ASSERT `s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the requirement was to give an explanation or a statement, not to produce books: the gate "in respect of a requirement to produce any books" fails
-- (test alias a8a8 = `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`)
-- arguments: provided an explanation or statement in purported compliance; it is false or misleading in a material particular; the person knew; the person was reckless
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "which the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular"
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is false or misleading in a material particular"
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- false but neither knew nor reckless: an element is unmet (split site (i))
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not false or misleading in a material particular
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not provided in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A
-- (test alias a8a8p = `s 8A(8) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`)
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 20000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both" (24 months)
#ASSERT `s 8A(8) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty: no penalty stated

§ `Regulative rules of s 8A`
-- s 8A(6): the duty a requirement imposes, with the time the requirement specifies (here 14 days after the requirement was imposed).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 8A(6) the person on whom a requirement was imposed must comply with it` (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 8A(6) comply with a requirement to produce books, provide an explanation or make a statement` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 8A(6) the person on whom a requirement was imposed must comply with it` (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") 14 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAITUNTIL` 15)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8A(6) the person on whom a requirement was imposed must comply with it` (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") 14 AT 0 WITH
-- s 8A(8): the prohibition derived from the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 8A(8) a person must not provide a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` "Ravi" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ravi" DOES `s 8A(8) provide in purported compliance an explanation or statement that is false or misleading in a material particular` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8A(8) a person must not provide a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` "Ravi" AT 0 WITH

§ `s 8B(1) to (3): the warrant`
-- (test alias a8b1 = `s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books`)
-- arguments: information laid on oath or affirmation by an authorised person; the Magistrate is satisfied there are reasonable grounds for suspecting books required under 8A are on the premises; those books have not been produced
#ASSERT `s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "If a Magistrate is satisfied, on information on oath or affirmation laid by an authorised person, that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting ... the Magistrate may issue a warrant"
#ASSERT `s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- information not laid by an authorised person: a failed "if" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the Magistrate is not satisfied: a failed "if" gating a grant
#ASSERT `s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books have been produced: a failed "if" gating a grant
-- (test alias a8b2 = `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- issued 10 March 2025, asked on the day it was issued: in force ("continues in force until the end of the period of one month after the date on which it was issued")
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of one month after 10 March is 10 April: in force on 10 April
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 11 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later: the period fixed in the text's own words has ended (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day before it was issued: outside the period
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- issued 31 January: one month after is 28 February (P4: the month's last day), in force on 28 February
#ASSERT `s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 1 March is after the last day, 28 February
-- (test alias a8b3 = `s 8B(3) the taking of possession of the books, or the securing of them against interference, prejudices the lien`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(3) the taking of possession of the books, or the securing of them against interference, prejudices the lien` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the taking of possession of the books or the securing of the books against interference does not prejudice the lien"
#ASSERT `s 8B(3) the taking of possession of the books, or the securing of them against interference, prejudices the lien` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no one has a lien: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `s 8B(3) the taking of possession of the books, or the securing of them against interference, prejudices the lien` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- books not taken or secured under section 8B

§ `s 8B(4) to (6)`
-- (test alias a8b4 = `s 8B(4) the person has the power`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(4) the person has the power` `s 8B(4)(a) make copies of, or take extracts from, the books` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) may make copies of, or take extracts from, the books"
#ASSERT `s 8B(4) the person has the power` `s 8B(4)(b) require a person who was party to the compilation of the books to make a statement providing an explanation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) may require any person who was party to the compilation of the books to make a statement"
#ASSERT `s 8B(4) the person has the power` `s 8B(4)(c) retain possession of the books for such period as is necessary for their inspection and for copies or extracts to be made by or on behalf of the Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) may retain possession of the books for such period as is necessary"
#ASSERT `s 8B(4) the person has the power` `s 8B(4)(a) make copies of, or take extracts from, the books` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person neither took possession nor holds delivered books: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
-- (test alias a8b4d = `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the person entitled to inspect to inspect the books at all reasonable times`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the person entitled to inspect to inspect the books at all reasonable times` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "during that period must permit a person who would be entitled to inspect any one or more of those books ... to inspect at all reasonable times"
#ASSERT `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the person entitled to inspect to inspect the books at all reasonable times` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person is not one who would be entitled to inspect: the duty's own question
#ASSERT `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the person entitled to inspect to inspect the books at all reasonable times` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside the period of retention: the duty's own question
-- (test alias a8b5 = `s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section"
#ASSERT `s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or who obstructs the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books"
#ASSERT `s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither: an element is unmet (split site (i))
-- (test alias a8b5p = `s 8B(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 6, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
#ASSERT `s 8B(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty
-- (test alias a8b6 = `s 8B(6) the powers conferred by section 8B derogate from the other power`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(6) the powers conferred by section 8B derogate from the other power` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "The powers conferred by this section are in addition to, and not in derogation of, any other power conferred by law"
#ASSERT `s 8B(6) the powers conferred by section 8B derogate from the other power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no other power conferred by law
-- s 8B(5): the prohibition derived from the offence; s 8B(4)(d): the duty, which has no time limit and no stated consequence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 8B(5) a person must not obstruct a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant` "Kim" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Kim" DOES `s 8B(5) obstruct the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by a warrant, or the exercise of a right to take possession of any books` AT 1
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8B(5) a person must not obstruct a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant` "Kim" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the inspection` "Sam" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Sam" DOES `s 8B(4)(d) permit a person entitled to inspect the books to inspect them at all reasonable times` AT 30
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the inspection` "Sam" AT 0 WITH

§ `s 8C: copies and extracts as evidence`
-- (test alias a8c1 = `s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it`)
-- arguments: legal proceedings; a copy of or extract from a book relating to the affairs of a corporation; it is proved to be a true copy
#ASSERT `s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "a copy of or extract from a book relating to the affairs of a corporation is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book"
#ASSERT `s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not admissible in evidence under subsection (1) unless it is proved that the copy or extract is a true copy"
#ASSERT `s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not legal proceedings: subsection (1) does not speak
#ASSERT `s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a copy of a book relating to the affairs of a corporation: subsection (1) does not speak
-- (test alias a8c3 = `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy`)
#ASSERT `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` TRUE `s 8C(3) orally` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "may be given by a person who has compared the copy or extract with the book ... either orally"
#ASSERT `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` TRUE `s 8C(3) by an affidavit sworn before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or by an affidavit sworn ... before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations"
#ASSERT `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` TRUE `s 8C(3) by a declaration made before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or by a declaration made, before a person authorised"
#ASSERT `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` TRUE `s 8C(3) in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another way: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` FALSE `s 8C(3) orally` EQUALS NOTHING   -- evidence from a person who has not compared the copy: the text says nothing

§ `s 8D: destroying, mutilating or falsifying documents`
-- (test alias a8d4 = `s 8D(4) the person is within the words officer of a corporation`)
#ASSERT `s 8D(4) the person is within the words officer of a corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) was at any time an officer of the corporation"
#ASSERT `s 8D(4) the person is within the words officer of a corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) has, or had, a financial or other interest in the affairs of the corporation"
#ASSERT `s 8D(4) the person is within the words officer of a corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "includes": the list is open
-- (test alias a8d1 = `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`)
-- arguments: officer of the corporation (as (4) uses the words); section 8A(1) applies to the corporation; destroyed, mutilated or falsified, or privy; made or was privy to a false entry; proves no intention to conceal or defeat the law
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- destroys, mutilates or falsifies, with no proof of innocent intention
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or makes or is privy to the making of a false entry in such a document"
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the officer proves that he or she had no intention to conceal the affairs of the corporation or to defeat the law"
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- section 8A(1) does not apply to the corporation: an element is unmet (split site (i))
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an officer: an element is unmet
#ASSERT `s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- did none of the acts: an element is unmet
-- (test alias a8d2 = `s 8D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`)
#ASSERT `s 8D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A person to whom subsection (1) applies who fraudulently either parts with, alters or makes an omission in any such document"
#ASSERT `s 8D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not fraudulent: an element is unmet
#ASSERT `s 8D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a person to whom (1) applies: an element is unmet
-- (test alias a8d3 = `s 8D(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction`)
#ASSERT `s 8D(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both"
#ASSERT `s 8D(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 8D(1) an officer must not destroy, mutilate or falsify a company document, or make a false entry in it` "Mei" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Officer "Mei" DOES `s 8D(1) destroy, mutilate or falsify a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or make a false entry in it` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8D(1) an officer must not destroy, mutilate or falsify a company document, or make a false entry in it` "Mei" AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 8D(2) a person must not fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in a company document` "Mei" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Officer "Mei" DOES `s 8D(2) fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in such a document` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 8D(2) a person must not fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in a company document` "Mei" AT 0 WITH

§ `The seam: s 4(8) asks whether the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402`
-- (test alias a8seam = `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D`)
#ASSERT `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` "8A" EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 8A is one of the listed sections
#ASSERT `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` "8C" EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 8C
#ASSERT `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` "8D" EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 8D
#ASSERT `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` "8B" EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 8B is not in the list s 4(8) names
#ASSERT `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` "216" EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 216 is another part's section
